{title: Midnight Ferry & the Gulls}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[Bb]Midnight ferry o[F]n the water
[Gm]Gulls asleep on [Eb]every rail
[Bb]Captain's humming like h[F]is father
[Gm]Every night – th[Eb]e same old tale [F]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Rock me, ferry b[Bb]oat
[F]Carry me across <t[Gm]he> tide
[Eb]Rock me, ferry b[Bb]oat
[F]Till I reach the ot[Bb]her side
{end_of_chorus}
